   {
    "text": "(Verse 1)  \nI’ve been watching kids play,  \nThey chase the ball, they laugh so loud,  \nBut the playground’s just a rusted old shed,  \nNo swings, no slides, no fun at all.  \n\n(Chorus)  \nSo let’s build a new playground,  \nWith swings that swing, and slides that slide,  \nWhere kids can run, and play, and ride,  \nA place where dreams can’t hide.  \n\n(Verse 2)  \nWe’ll paint the walls with colors bright,  \nAdd a slide that’s tall and tight,  \nA sandbox where the sand is bright,  \nAnd a slide that’s fun, not tight.  \n\n(Chorus)  \nSo let’s build a new playground,  \nWith swings that swing, and slides that slide,  \nWhere kids can run, and play, and ride,  \nA place where dreams can’t hide.  \n\n(Outro)  \nBecause kids need more than just a shed,  \nThey need a place to play, to grow, to spread.  \nSo let’s build it now, and make it great,  \nA playground where the future’s made.",
